# Aston Martin DB9 coupe, 2004-2016.
#
# The VH-platform DB9 by Ian Callum and Henrik Fisker: the long bonnet, the
# wide mesh grille, the pronounced rear haunches and the twin exhausts. The
# coupe is modelled; the Volante is a different body. The car photographed is
# the pre-facelift 2004-08 car.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aston_Martin_DB9
#
# Dimensions 4.697-4.720 m long x 1.875 m wide excluding mirrors (2.017-2.061
# including mirrors) x 1.270-1.282 m high, wheelbase 2.740 m. 1.875 m is used,
# the mirror width being excluded as on every other car in the pakset.
#
# Shape reference: a dark blue DB9 coupe in true level side elevation, front
# three-quarter and rear three-quarter. One car throughout.
#
# Colours: grade (a) for the 2012 model year only, from the Aston Martin
# Colour & Trim UK brochure (part 705699): Midnight Blue, Tungsten Silver,
# Volcano Red and Jet Black. Earlier lists were not found. Weights 3, 3, 2, 2,
# total 10, provisional.
#
# Speed 300 km/h. Comfort 80/450, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 80. Classes 3,4.
# Dates are road presence: 2004 intro, retires staggered 2032-2036.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/aston-db9.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/aston-db9.dae. References:
# citycars/references/aston-db9/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear lenses distort around the corners and the
# plate recess is too rounded. At 128 px the long bonnet, wide grille and
# haunches read as a DB9.


